\title{Landmarking of a Survival Task with a Longitudinal Table}
\description{
Creates a \emph{landmark dataset} from a survival task (\code{TaskSurv}) and a subject-level longitudinal
table (\code{long}). At a given \code{landmark_time}, the PipeOp:
\itemize{
\item keeps only subjects still at risk (\code{time > landmark_time}),
\item rebases survival time by subtracting \code{landmark_time},
\item filters longitudinal rows to those subjects and measurements taken at or before the landmark,
\item (optionally) drops subjects without enough longitudinal information (\code{min_points}).
}

The filtered longitudinal table is returned on a second output channel and is given class \code{"Long"}.
}
\details{
This PipeOp expects the input task to have exactly one group column (subject identifier) set via
\code{task$col_roles$group}. The survival target is assumed to be in the order returned by
\code{task$target_names}, where the first target is the time column and the second target is the event
column.

If \code{long_features} is \code{NULL}, numeric longitudinal feature columns are auto-detected from \code{long}
(excluding \code{long_id_col} and \code{long_time_col}).
}
